Compute Engine — Dependency Notice

The Polymer Genomics methylation compute engine depends on R packages released
under the GNU General Public License (GPL-2 and GPL-3), including packages from
the Bioconductor project (minfi, sesame, limma, ComplexHeatmap, and others).

If you redistribute the engine Dockerfile or the container image built from it,
you must comply with the GPL terms of those dependencies. In particular, you must
make the source code of the GPL-licensed packages available to recipients upon
request, as required by the GPL.

The Polymer Genomics source code itself (outside of these dependencies) is
licensed under the MIT License. See the root LICENSE file.

For the full text of the GPL, see: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html
